```

Identical text at [list_missing_blobs.rs:153](crates/pds/src/routes/list_missing_blobs.rs:153) and [check_account_status.rs:151](crates/pds/src/routes/check_account_status.rs:151). `cargo fmt -p pds --check` and `cargo clippy -p pds --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean against the worktree manifest.

On the ticket-vs-upstream point — noted, that's yours. The PR body still names it as an open follow-up, so it won't vanish silently even though "Fixes MM-473" closes the ticket on merge.

Your two nits I agreed with and left alone: `Scan::Take(String)` allocates exactly where the old `strip` did (making it borrow would fight the `.await` across the loop body for no measurable gain), and a key of exactly `"collection/"` yielding an empty rkey isn't reachable through any validated write path — `validate_record_path` rejects an empty rkey, and an imported CAR carrying one would already be malformed upstream of this function.
